/* zh-SG translation source for "endings" (generated by tools/i18n-pack.js; keys are the English source). */
Object.assign(window.I18N['zh-SG'].text, {
  "★ True End": "★ 真结局",
  "Plain Love": "平凡的爱",
  "One year after the A-levels. Hanis is deep into her nursing degree. You are deep into {passion}, your course and your own plans. Neither of you shrank to fit the other.\nYou still meet at the dragon playground at Seri Bayu. You still argue sometimes, then repair it before it sets. You know her real favourites, not the ones you guessed.\nOn your desk: a nasi lemak with the egg cut into a heart. On her phone: a budget you made together, and it balances.\nMochi, from the windowsill: \"Not fireworks. A fire you both keep lit. That's the good kind.\"": "A水准考完一年后。哈妮丝全心投入她的护理学位。你全心投入{passion}、你的课程和你自己的计划。你们谁都没有为了迁就对方而把自己缩小。\n你们还是会在斯里巴尤的龙形游乐场见面。你们有时还是会吵架，然后在它变成心结之前修复好。你知道她真正喜欢的东西，而不是你猜的那些。\n你的书桌上：一份椰浆饭，鸡蛋被切成了心形。她的手机上：一份你们一起做的预算，而且收支平衡。\n麻糬在窗台上说：“不是烟花。是一团你们两个一起守着的火。那才是好的那种。”",
  "Normal End": "普通结局",
  "Still Learning": "还在学习中",
  "Hanis and you are still together. Most days it is good. Some days one of you goes quiet instead of saying the hard thing, or the calendar has room for only one of your lives.\nNone of it is a disaster. All of it is a habit, and habits can change.\nMochi: \"You passed, rookie. Not with honours. Keep practising the boring parts: listening, repair, your own life. Those ARE the romantic parts.\"": "你和哈妮丝还在一起。大部分日子都很好。有些日子，你们其中一个人选择沉默，而不是说出那句难开口的话；或者日程表上只容得下你们其中一个人的生活。\n这些都不是灾难。全都是习惯，而习惯是可以改变的。\n麻糬：“你及格了，菜鸟。不是优等。继续练习那些无聊的部分：倾听、修复、你自己的生活。那些才是真正浪漫的部分。”",
  "Good End": "好结局",
  "A Kind Goodbye": "温柔的告别",
  "You and Hanis ended it in the year that tested everyone. Nobody screamed. Nobody posted anything. You said thank you, and you meant it.\nA year later she sends a photo from her nursing degree. You send one back from your own first real step with {passion}. You are both, quietly, better people than the two kids who met in JC1.\nMochi: \"Love that ends well is still love. You lost a girlfriend. You did not lose yourself. Good trade? No. Good person? Yes.\"": "在那个考验每一个人的年份里，你和哈妮丝结束了。没有人尖叫。没有人发帖。你说了谢谢，而且是真心的。\n一年后，她从护理系发来一张照片。你回了一张，是你在{passion}上真正迈出的第一步。你们两个都悄悄地，成为了比初院一年级相遇时那两个孩子更好的人。\n麻糬：“好好结束的爱，依然是爱。你失去了一个女朋友。你没有失去你自己。划算吗？不。是个好人吗？是的。”",
  "One year after the A-levels. Xin Yi is deep into her writing programme in Melbourne. You are deep into {passion}, your course and your own plans. Neither of you shrank to fit the other.\nYou still meet at the bookshop on the third floor of the mall. You still argue sometimes, then repair it before it sets. You know her real favourites, not the ones you guessed.\nOn your desk: a manuscript with your name in the acknowledgements, spelled right this time. On her phone: a budget you made together, and it balances.\nMochi, from the windowsill: \"Not fireworks. A fire you both keep lit. That's the good kind.\"": "A水准考完一年后。欣怡全心投入她在墨尔本的写作课程。你全心投入{passion}、你的课程和你自己的计划。你们谁都没有为了迁就对方而把自己缩小。\n你们还是会在商场三楼的书店见面。你们有时还是会吵架，然后在它变成心结之前修复好。你知道她真正喜欢的东西，而不是你猜的那些。\n你的书桌上：一份手稿，致谢里有你的名字，这次拼对了。她的手机上：一份你们一起做的预算，而且收支平衡。\n麻糬在窗台上说：“不是烟花。是一团你们两个一起守着的火。那才是好的那种。”",
  "Xin Yi and you are still together. Most days it is good. Some days one of you goes quiet instead of saying the hard thing, or the calendar has room for only one of your lives.\nNone of it is a disaster. All of it is a habit, and habits can change.\nMochi: \"You passed, rookie. Not with honours. Keep practising the boring parts: listening, repair, your own life. Those ARE the romantic parts.\"": "你和欣怡还在一起。大部分日子都很好。有些日子，你们其中一个人选择沉默，而不是说出那句难开口的话；或者日程表上只容得下你们其中一个人的生活。\n这些都不是灾难。全都是习惯，而习惯是可以改变的。\n麻糬：“你及格了，菜鸟。不是优等。继续练习那些无聊的部分：倾听、修复、你自己的生活。那些才是真正浪漫的部分。”",
  "You and Xin Yi ended it in the year that tested everyone. Nobody screamed. Nobody posted anything. You said thank you, and you meant it.\nA year later she sends a photo from her writing programme in Melbourne. You send one back from your own first real step with {passion}. You are both, quietly, better people than the two kids who met in JC1.\nMochi: \"Love that ends well is still love. You lost a girlfriend. You did not lose yourself. Good trade? No. Good person? Yes.\"": "在那个考验每一个人的年份里，你和欣怡结束了。没有人尖叫。没有人发帖。你说了谢谢，而且是真心的。\n一年后，她从墨尔本的写作课程发来一张照片。你回了一张，是你在{passion}上真正迈出的第一步。你们两个都悄悄地，成为了比初院一年级相遇时那两个孩子更好的人。\n麻糬：“好好结束的爱，依然是爱。你失去了一个女朋友。你没有失去你自己。划算吗？不。是个好人吗？是的。”",
  "One year after the A-levels. Kavya is deep into her athletics scholarship. You are deep into {passion}, your course and your own plans. Neither of you shrank to fit the other.\nYou still meet at the track at dawn. You still argue sometimes, then repair it before it sets. You know her real favourites, not the ones you guessed.\nOn your desk: a race bib from her first college meet, mailed with a sticky note: \"you waited, I ran\". On her phone: a budget you made together, and it balances.\nMochi, from the windowsill: \"Not fireworks. A fire you both keep lit. That's the good kind.\"": "A水准考完一年后。卡维娅全心投入她的田径奖学金生活。你全心投入{passion}、你的课程和你自己的计划。你们谁都没有为了迁就对方而把自己缩小。\n你们还是会在清晨的跑道上见面。你们有时还是会吵架，然后在它变成心结之前修复好。你知道她真正喜欢的东西，而不是你猜的那些。\n你的书桌上：一张她第一场大学比赛的号码布，寄来时贴着一张便利贴：“你等了，我跑了”。她的手机上：一份你们一起做的预算，而且收支平衡。\n麻糬在窗台上说：“不是烟花。是一团你们两个一起守着的火。那才是好的那种。”",
  "Kavya and you are still together. Most days it is good. Some days one of you goes quiet instead of saying the hard thing, or the calendar has room for only one of your lives.\nNone of it is a disaster. All of it is a habit, and habits can change.\nMochi: \"You passed, rookie. Not with honours. Keep practising the boring parts: listening, repair, your own life. Those ARE the romantic parts.\"": "你和卡维娅还在一起。大部分日子都很好。有些日子，你们其中一个人选择沉默，而不是说出那句难开口的话；或者日程表上只容得下你们其中一个人的生活。\n这些都不是灾难。全都是习惯，而习惯是可以改变的。\n麻糬：“你及格了，菜鸟。不是优等。继续练习那些无聊的部分：倾听、修复、你自己的生活。那些才是真正浪漫的部分。”",
  "You and Kavya ended it in the year that tested everyone. Nobody screamed. Nobody posted anything. You said thank you, and you meant it.\nA year later she sends a photo from her athletics scholarship. You send one back from your own first real step with {passion}. You are both, quietly, better people than the two kids who met in JC1.\nMochi: \"Love that ends well is still love. You lost a girlfriend. You did not lose yourself. Good trade? No. Good person? Yes.\"": "在那个考验每一个人的年份里，你和卡维娅结束了。没有人尖叫。没有人发帖。你说了谢谢，而且是真心的。\n一年后，她从田径奖学金的学校发来一张照片。你回了一张，是你在{passion}上真正迈出的第一步。你们两个都悄悄地，成为了比初院一年级相遇时那两个孩子更好的人。\n麻糬：“好好结束的爱，依然是爱。你失去了一个女朋友。你没有失去你自己。划算吗？不。是个好人吗？是的。”",
  "One year after the A-levels. Elise is deep into her dance academy in Seoul. You are deep into {passion}, your course and your own plans. Neither of you shrank to fit the other.\nYou still meet at a quiet table at a hawker centre, no camera. You still argue sometimes, then repair it before it sets. You know her real favourites, not the ones you guessed.\nOn your desk: a photo that was never posted, just printed and kept. On her phone: a budget you made together, and it balances.\nMochi, from the windowsill: \"Not fireworks. A fire you both keep lit. That's the good kind.\"": "A水准考完一年后。伊莉丝全心投入她在首尔的舞蹈学院。你全心投入{passion}、你的课程和你自己的计划。你们谁都没有为了迁就对方而把自己缩小。\n你们还是会在小贩中心一张安静的桌子旁见面，没有镜头。你们有时还是会吵架，然后在它变成心结之前修复好。你知道她真正喜欢的东西，而不是你猜的那些。\n你的书桌上：一张从来没有发布过的照片，只是洗出来收好。她的手机上：一份你们一起做的预算，而且收支平衡。\n麻糬在窗台上说：“不是烟花。是一团你们两个一起守着的火。那才是好的那种。”",
  "Elise and you are still together. Most days it is good. Some days one of you goes quiet instead of saying the hard thing, or the calendar has room for only one of your lives.\nNone of it is a disaster. All of it is a habit, and habits can change.\nMochi: \"You passed, rookie. Not with honours. Keep practising the boring parts: listening, repair, your own life. Those ARE the romantic parts.\"": "你和伊莉丝还在一起。大部分日子都很好。有些日子，你们其中一个人选择沉默，而不是说出那句难开口的话；或者日程表上只容得下你们其中一个人的生活。\n这些都不是灾难。全都是习惯，而习惯是可以改变的。\n麻糬：“你及格了，菜鸟。不是优等。继续练习那些无聊的部分：倾听、修复、你自己的生活。那些才是真正浪漫的部分。”",
  "You and Elise ended it in the year that tested everyone. Nobody screamed. Nobody posted anything. You said thank you, and you meant it.\nA year later she sends a photo from her dance academy in Seoul. You send one back from your own first real step with {passion}. You are both, quietly, better people than the two kids who met in JC1.\nMochi: \"Love that ends well is still love. You lost a girlfriend. You did not lose yourself. Good trade? No. Good person? Yes.\"": "在那个考验每一个人的年份里，你和伊莉丝结束了。没有人尖叫。没有人发帖。你说了谢谢，而且是真心的。\n一年后，她从首尔的舞蹈学院发来一张照片。你回了一张，是你在{passion}上真正迈出的第一步。你们两个都悄悄地，成为了比初院一年级相遇时那两个孩子更好的人。\n麻糬：“好好结束的爱，依然是爱。你失去了一个女朋友。你没有失去你自己。划算吗？不。是个好人吗？是的。”",
  "★ Best End": "★ 最佳结局",
  "Your grades got you where you wanted. {passion} turned into something real: a first gig, a first show, a first release. You sleep. You save. You are kind to your family and honest with everyone.\nWhoever you are with, or not with, you are a whole person. People are drawn to that without you ever trying to be impressive.\nMochi: \"This was the secret all along: love doesn't complete you. You show up complete, and love is what you share.\"": "你的成绩带你去了你想去的地方。{passion}变成了真实的东西：第一场演出、第一次展出、第一次发布。你有好好睡觉。你有存钱。你对家人很好，对每个人都很诚实。\n不管你身边有没有人，你都是一个完整的人。人们会被这一点吸引，而你从来不需要刻意去让人印象深刻。\n麻糬：“这一直都是那个秘密：爱不会让你变完整。你带着完整的自己出现，而爱是你们分享的东西。”",
  "Lesson End": "教训结局",
  "Side Character in Your Own Life": "自己人生里的配角",
  "You gave everything to love: your grades, your sleep, your savings, {passion}. Somewhere along the way you became a supporting role in someone else's story, and then not even that.\nThis is not a punishment. It is a mirror. Nobody can love a person who is not there.\nMochi: \"New Game+, rookie. This time, play the main character. Hint: the main character has a life.\"": "你把一切都给了爱情：你的成绩、你的睡眠、你的储蓄、{passion}。不知不觉中，你变成了别人故事里的配角，后来连配角都不是了。\n这不是惩罚。这是一面镜子。没有人能去爱一个不在场的人。\n麻糬：“二周目吧，菜鸟。这一次，当主角。提示：主角是有自己的生活的。”",
  "Whole Person": "完整的人",
  "No girlfriend at the end of this story, and that is fine. You have friends who would help you move house, a passion that pays a little, a body that runs 5K, and a bank account that is not on fire.\nAt a friend's book launch, someone laughs at the same moment you do. You talk for an hour. You get her number the normal way: by asking.\nMochi: \"Not a consolation prize. A head start.\"": "这个故事的结尾没有女朋友，而这没关系。你有会帮你搬家的朋友、一份能赚一点钱的热爱、一副能跑五公里的身体，还有一个没有着火的银行户口。\n在一个朋友的新书发布会上，有个人和你在同一个瞬间笑了出来。你们聊了一个小时。你用最正常的方式拿到了她的电话号码：开口问。\n麻糬：“这不是安慰奖。这是领先起跑。”",
  "Still Searching": "还在寻找",
  "Alone, and not the good kind of alone yet. Some lessons stuck. Some didn't. You still check her stories sometimes.\nBut you are nineteen. Nothing is decided. The chess uncles at the void deck have been losing to each other for forty years and they still show up every evening.\nMochi: \"New Game+ starts now. I'm not giving up on you. Don't you dare give up on you.\"": "一个人，而且还不是那种好的一个人。有些课学进去了。有些没有。你有时还是会去看她的限时动态。\n但你才十九岁。什么都还没定下来。组屋楼下下象棋的安哥们已经互相输了四十年，他们还是每天傍晚都来。\n麻糬：“二周目现在开始。我不会放弃你。你也不准放弃你自己。”",
  "Comic Good End": "搞笑好结局",
  "Prata Brothers": "煎饼兄弟",
  "You and Haziq go halves on a stall in the Seri Bayu hawker centre: \"Bro Prata\". The egg prata is excellent. The business plan was written on a tissue.\nIt works, mostly because you both actually show up, do the books on Sunday and never lend money to Ryan.\nMochi: \"Platonic love is still love. Also, I want the plain prata. With fish curry. Free.\"": "你和哈齐克合伙在斯里巴尤小贩中心开了一个摊位：“兄弟煎饼”。鸡蛋煎饼非常好吃。商业计划书是写在纸巾上的。\n生意做起来了，主要是因为你们两个真的天天都到场、每个星期天都对账，而且从来不借钱给瑞安。\n麻糬：“友情的爱也是爱。还有，我要一片原味煎饼。配鱼咖喱。免费的。”",
  "Side Ending": "支线结局",
  "Rae, For Real": "瑞儿，真正的她",
  "Rae testified. The \"agency\" is gone, and so is Mr. G. She works at a café now, studies at night and gives talks to younger students about scam scripts.\nYou are friends. Real ones, with boundaries. She says you were the first person who helped her without trying to buy her.": "瑞儿出庭作证了。那家“经纪公司”不在了，G先生也不在了。她现在在一家咖啡馆工作，晚上读书，还会给年纪更小的学生讲骗局剧本。\n你们是朋友。真正的朋友，有界线的那种。她说你是第一个帮她、却没有想用钱“买”她的人。",
  "Secret Ending": "隐藏结局",
  "Mochi Graduates": "麻糬毕业了",
  "Almost every page of the notebook is filled. Mochi closes it, adjusts her tiny glasses and passes her Love Guide exam with distinction.\n\"Thank you, rookie. You were my thesis.\" She considers. \"Your mistakes were very educational. Some were also very funny.\"": "笔记本几乎每一页都写满了。麻糬合上它，扶了扶她的小眼镜，以优异的成绩通过了她的恋爱指南考试。\n“谢谢你，菜鸟。你是我的毕业论文。”她想了想。“你的错误非常有教育意义。有些也非常好笑。”"
});
